Choose [Buddhism](buddhism/Buddhism.lingua#r_7P61Z6HHZNZZ8ND3DHXSFSNRRE) for the ordered reading from Bhikkhu Bodhi’s account of the path through the discourse collections and later traditions. Choose [Yoga](yoga/Yoga.lingua#r_017AAD0FQ294F8HBVVTQAZ55GH) for a short reading of Iyengar’s Light on Yoga.

These are separate entrances into questions concerning action, discipline, knowledge, suffering, and liberation. Their grouping provides a place to find and compare them; it does not establish that their accounts of karma, self, practice, or liberation are identical.

Return to [Philosophy](../Philosophy.lingua#r_00000000000000000000001001) for shared questions and reading methods. Follow the particular `#buddhism` or `#yoga` assertions for its learning connections. Sources and optional comparisons use their own references.

